calc_check.py:370:    # [46i.1] a range summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and no figure reads it\ncalc_check.py:424:        for f in figs.values():                       # [46i.1] scenario membership is derived along the whole path, not declared\ncalc_check.py:447:        for f in sorted(later_graph):                 # [46k.1] every later scenario path reaches the earlier forecast of its own scenario\ncalc_check.py:453:                errors.append(('C9', f'{f} ({sc}) of {rel[\"later\"]} does not rest on {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s {sc} forecast'))\ncalc_check.py:455:            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} does not rest on {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast ({\", \".join(sorted(earlier_nodes))})'))\ncalc_check.py:457:            errors.append(('C9', f'{rel[\"later\"]} reaches {\", \".join(sorted(bypass))} for {base_key} without {rel[\"earlier\"]}\\'s forecast'))\ncalc_check.py:460:        earlier = fig['kind'] == 'prior' or fig.get('basis') == 'prior_forecast' or 'pointer' in fig   # [46i.2] derived, not labelled\ncalc_check.py:493:def changed(previous, answer, figs):\ncalc_check.py:501:    own = _upstream_of(out['id'], figs, refs) | {out['id']}                  # [46k.3] the member's own outcome and reference only\nDESIGN.md:1:# judging-v13: related number questions judged together, with a checked calculation (design v10, after council round 46j and D728; for round 46k)\nDESIGN.md:57:  forecast node of the earlier member at the same snapshot (q22 reads q01's): C9.\nDESIGN.md:80:| **C4 scenarios** [46g.3, 46h.1, 46i.1] | each scenario has one forecast node per shared quantity. Scenario membership is derived along the whole path: no figure of a point scenario may depend, at any depth, on a forecast node of another scenario. A `range` summary is an estimate with low and high, is an answer's outcome, and feeds no figure; only it may rest on several scenarios; a bypass is a path that reaches the quantity through no forecast node of any scenario | a low path on the high total; a guide relabelled as an alternate scenario and read by the base |\nDESIGN.md:83:| **C9 same base** [46f.3, 46j.2] | for each `same_base(later, earlier)`, the later member rests on the earlier member's forecast nodes (its outcome, or the scenario paths behind its range summary), and every path to a figure of the earlier quantity and period passes through one of them; scenarios match by C4 | FY2028 grown from the $392B consensus instead of q01's $400–435B forecast |\nDESIGN.md:84:| **C10 earlier forecasts** [46f.3, 46f.4, 46h.2, 46i.2] | a figure is an earlier forecast when its kind is prior, its basis is prior_forecast or it carries a pointer (derived, not labelled), and it must then be kind prior with basis prior_forecast; such a figure points to an earlier answer shown in the request and equals a figure that answer states; it feeds no figure and is no answer's outcome | an invented or misdated earlier figure; an earlier forecast used as an input |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
