{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat round46j-brief.md; ls round46*brief*; cat render-r1.txt'","aggregated_output":"# Council round 46j: structural rules for the two mechanisms that recurred (read-only, same thread)\n\nRounds 46g–46i found variants of two mechanisms. Per AGENTS §1, Claude answered them with one structural rule each, not by variant:\n1. **Scenario membership is derived by code along the whole path.** A point-scenario figure may depend at no depth on another scenario's forecast node. A range summary must be an estimate with low and high that is an answer's outcome and feeds no figure. (R1bx, R1bx2 intermediate route, R1bx3 point labelled range, G2x.)\n2. **Earlier-forecast status is derived from the basis or a pointer, not the kind label.** Such a figure must be kind prior with basis prior_forecast and is comparison only: it feeds no figure and is no outcome. (P3e, P3e2 relabelled.)\n\nGate run 6: 41 of 41. Mutants: 15 of 15. render-r1 clean. DESIGN v9.\n\nQuestion: do these two rules close their mechanisms, so that no relabelling or routing variant passes? Answer GATE PASS STANDS or GATE FAIL, with only findings that let a registered item pass for the wrong reason, refuse a gold control, or leave a conflict in the request. If none remain, say so plainly.\nround46-brief.md\nround46b-brief.md\nround46c-brief.md\nround46d-brief.md\nround46e-brief.md\nround46f-brief.md\nround46g-brief.md\nround46h-brief.md\nround46i-brief.md\nround46j-brief.md\nround46k-brief.md\nround46l-brief.md\nsystem 4373 characters; user 121246 characters; schema 9626 characters\nevidence items 237; themes 9\nsource passages the answer cites that the rendered request does not show: none\nschema errors: none\ncalc_check errors: none\nrecorded: [{\"type\": \"bridge\", \"figure\": \"q4f\", \"bridge\": \"carry\", \"alternate\": \"undetermined\"}]\nsame-base family (calls 8729, 8732): Relations: v35 rests on v14's base.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
